  "code": "CTs",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Significance</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Within Normal Range</strong> (usually <strong>2&ndash;15 minutes</strong>, method dependent: Lee &amp; White / Capillary tube)</td>\n<td>Normal coagulation cascade function.</td>\n<td>Suggests no major deficiency in intrinsic/common coagulation pathways.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Prolonged Clotting Time</strong></td>\n<td>Abnormal &ndash; indicates delayed clot formation.</td>\n<td>- Possible intrinsic pathway defects (Hemophilia A &ndash; Factor VIII deficiency, Hemophilia B &ndash; Factor IX deficiency, Factor XI deficiency) - Severe liver disease (affects clotting factor synthesis) - Vitamin K deficiency (affects II, VII, IX, X synthesis) - Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC) - Anticoagulant therapy (e.g., heparin) - Severe thrombocytopenia.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Shortened Clotting Time</strong> (rare)</td>\n<td>Faster than normal clot formation.</td>\n<td>Not usually clinically significant; may be due to a hypercoagulable state, technical error, or increased clotting factor activity.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
